# The release identity hashes the bytes of the pinned sources on disk, on purpose,
# so that a line-ending change shows up instead of hiding. That makes checkout
# behaviour part of the reproduction: with core.autocrlf=true and no attributes,
# git stores LF and hands out CRLF, so a fresh clone on Windows builds a different
# release id than the one committed in the pinned profile — and the clean-room
# reproduction never noticed, because it copied a working tree instead of cloning.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes every checkout produce the same bytes on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must not be touched at all.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
